### Effect ###
	Index        Effect ID (matches EFFECT_* constants in code).
	Group        Effects in the same Group replace each other (only
	           one active per Group at a time).
	ItemIndex    Item that grants this effect on use (GET_ITEM(12,x) -
	           matches Item.xml Index for Type 12 consumables), -1 if
	           not item-granted (a skill/passive/system state).
	Name         Display name.
	Save         1 = effect persists across relog (saved to DB).
	Type         0 = normal buff, 1 = item-use buff, 2 = Seal/Scroll/
	           Elixir/Talisman-style buff (adds stats via Value1-4).
	Flag         1 = debuff (shows as a negative/red state client-side).
	Count        Default duration in seconds, -1 = not time-limited.
	Value1-4     Stat bonus(es) this effect grants while active. What
	           each slot means is hardcoded PER INDEX in
	           CEffectManager::InsertEffect() (EffectManager.cpp) -
	           it is NOT a generic/uniform meaning across rows. See the
	           reference table below for every Index that actually
	           reads Value1-4; any Index not listed there ignores them
	           entirely (leave as -1).
	Value1Stat-4Stat   OPTIONAL. Makes that Value slot data-driven instead
	           of hardcoded: put the exact name of a field from struct
	           EFFECT_OPTION (User.h) here, e.g. Value1Stat="AddDefense",
	           and CEffectManager adds/subtracts Value1 to/from that stat
	           directly - no C++ case needed. This is how you create a
	           brand-new Seal/Scroll combo (see Index 206 below) without
	           touching code. ONLY use this on a NEW Index that has no
	           existing case in InsertEffect() - using it on one of the
	           already-hardcoded effects below would apply the value
	           twice (once via the switch, once via this). Leave empty
	           (or omit) for every effect that's already in the
	           reference table.

